\s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1 \'80(NSString *)\b name\
\fs14\
\b0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Returns the name of the notification. Examples of this might be \'aaPortIsInvalid\'ba or \'aaPhoneRinging.\'ba Typically, you invoke this method on the notification object passed to your notification-handler method. (You specify a notification-handler method when you register to receive the notification.) \
\fs14\
\fs28 Notification names can be any string. To avoid name collisions, however, you might want to use a prefix that\'27s specific to your application.\
\fs14\
